cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or methodology, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DNN-Derived Synthetic Vegetation Index for Phenotype Prediction"
abstract: >
  A deep neural network with a spectral bottleneck architecture learns a
  data-optimised vegetation index from raw multispectral UAV bands for
  agronomic trait prediction in winter barley. The single-neuron bottleneck
  (Synthetic VI) mimics the structure of hand-crafted indices (e.g. NDVI)
  while learning non-linear, trait-specific band combinations. Evaluated
  under leave-one-environment-out and within-environment cross-validation,
  with NDVI linear regression as a baseline and two transfer-learning
  adaptation strategies.
